# Development Guidelines

## Code Style and Standards

- Use type hints for all function parameters and return values
- Follow PEP 8 style guidelines
- Use descriptive variable and function names
- Add docstrings for all public functions and classes
- Use async/await for all database operations

## Database Operations

- Always use the async session from [db/session.py](mdc:db/session.py)
- Use proper error handling for database operations
- Follow the pattern in [db/models.py](mdc:db/models.py) for model definitions
- Use Alembic for all database schema changes

## Bot Development

- Use aiogram 3.x patterns and best practices
- Implement proper error handling in all handlers
- Use FSM states for multi-step user interactions
- Follow the middleware pattern in [middlewares/](mdc:middlewares/)
- Use the screen pattern in [screens/](mdc:screens/) for UI components

## Configuration Management

- Use [config.py](mdc:config.py) for application configuration
- Use environment variables for sensitive data
- Follow the pattern in [options/](mdc:options/) for feature flags

## Testing and Quality

- Test all database migrations before deployment
- Use the Docker setup for consistent development environment
- Follow the logging patterns in [logging_config.py](mdc:logging_config.py)
- Validate all user inputs and handle errors gracefully